; MM-VAL-7's counting rule, on the one path that broke it: a SECOND
; `Str` header naming an existing owner must take a second share.
;
; `strSlice` has always done this (`Str.ax`'s `(__retain owner)`).
; `Sys.sysReadAll` did not: at EOF it answers a fresh header over the
; read buffer's bytes, naming the buffer's owner, and took no share -
; so two headers claimed one count. That is inert while nothing
; releases a `Str` header, and a use-after-free the day something
; does (MM-LIFE-2e's extension work): the first release frees a
; buffer the other header still points into, and the block is on a
; size-class free list, so the next allocation re-issues it.
;
; This fixture asserts the COUNT, not a byte, because the bytes are
; identical either way - which is exactly why the defect survived
; being written.
;
;   32  the file round-trips: 5 bytes back out of sysReadFile
;   16  the answer's owner is a real block (not a literal's 0)
;    8  that owner's count word reads 2 - one share for the buffer
;       header strAlloc made, one for the header sysReadAll answered
;    4  a slice of the answer takes a third: count 3
;    2  the file is gone again
;    1  and nothing above was skipped
;
; 63 fixed. Against the unfixed standard library the same run reads
; the count as 1 and the slice's as 2, so both count terms fail and
; it answers 51 - the two terms that measure the share are exactly
; the two the fix adds.
(import Sys)
(import Str)

(:: b2i (-> Bool Int))
(fn (b2i x) (if x 1 0))

(:: ownerCount (-> String Int))
(fn (ownerCount s) (__load64 (- (strOwner s) 16) 0))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((f (strCStr "axiom_test_file_358"))
        (mut acc 0)
        (mut steps 0))
    {
      (sysWriteFile f "hello")
      (set steps (+ steps 1))
      (let ((got (sysReadFile f)))
        {
          (if (== (strLen got) 5) (set acc (+ acc 32)) 0)
          (if (!= (strOwner got) 0) (set acc (+ acc 16)) 0)
          (if (== (ownerCount got) 2) (set acc (+ acc 8)) 0)
          (let ((sl (strSlice got 1 3)))
            (if (== (ownerCount sl) 3) (set acc (+ acc 4)) 0))
          (set steps (+ steps 1))
        })
      (if (== (sysUnlink f) 0) (set acc (+ acc 2)) 0)
      (if (== steps 2) (set acc (+ acc 1)) 0)
      acc
    }))
